# deploy-pipeline.sh runs in this directory and writes all of its state here:
# execution chaindata, beacon datadirs, generated genesis, validator wallets and
# keys. A completed run reaches roughly a terabyte.
#
# So ignore everything and opt in to the tracked files by name. An allow-list is
# used rather than a list of generated paths because the cost of missing an entry
# is committing chaindata or a validator key, and new state directories appear
# whenever the stack count changes (data2/, cl-data3/, vcdata-*/ and so on).
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
!deploy-pipeline.sh
